#################################################################
#  v9.74.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- LINEAGE 9, Goal stage.
#  Consumes Out_Scope_SDLC (f586f36). Status moves to LS_Goaled.
#
#  WHAT THIS STAGE OWES, AND WHY IT IS NOT HERE. Under the obligation
#  this lineage is building, the Goal stage owes the USE CASES with
#  their main and alternative SCENARIOS -- the owner's own words. An
#  obligation names an artifact KIND by IRI, and this framework's scope
#  excludes minting kinds (Ex_SDLC_NoNewKinds, L-64). another registrant defines
#  five ArtifactKindSpecs today, all document kinds; none is a use
#  case, a scenario set, a behaviour diagram or a domain model. Four
#  were requested from another registrant in the previous commit (1b65620, their
#  inbox). Until they exist, the use cases cannot be typed, and a
#  use case written with no kind to point at is exactly the artifact
#  nobody can check -- the thing this lineage exists to end.
#  So: the goals are recorded now, the obligation is recorded as an
#  impediment, and the Goal stage's OWED ARTIFACTS are the first
#  work of the Objective and Backlog stages once the kinds exist.
#  Stated, not hidden (G7): this stage closes owing.
#################################################################



#################################################################
#  v9.75.0 (2026-09-09, brsf-session) -- THE OBLIGATIONS DO NOT BIND
#  THE LINEAGE THAT BUILDS THEM. Owner's rule, this day: "apply the
#  rulings only after the completion of the work and the lineage is
#  closed. You should never try to apply a new ruling when the
#  development is in progress."
#
#  The first draft of shapes v1.111.0 bound every lineage. Its first
#  run refused fw:Out_Goal_SDLC (published 629b62f) and four fixture
#  lineages and every toy of the exercise register -- work already
#  finished or in flight under rules that did not exist when it was
#  done. That is the same failure the owner named in an earlier
#  session, and the session repeated it. Corrected before release:
#  an obligation binds only a lineage that ADOPTED its set at the
#  moment it opened (adoptsObligationSet + adoptionRecordedAtOpen,
#  in the Mission stage's own commit), and ObligationAdoptionShape
#  refuses adoption by a lineage past LS_Opened. Lineage 9 is past
#  LS_Goaled; it therefore does not adopt and owes nothing new. The
#  first lineage OPENED after these obligations ship will be the
#  first to owe them.
#
#  Imp_SDLCArtifactKinds is RESOLVED BY FINDING: the four artifact
#  kinds requested from another registrant (1b65620) already existed in this
#  framework's own TBox -- ModelKind's fourteen UML 2.5 kinds,
#  Specification/InteractionStep/hasStepActor, TestScenario's four
#  ScenarioKinds, DomainEntity, Blueprint. Withdrawn the same day
#  (3c3dc13); analysis in 04-documentation/DECISION_ANALYSIS_sdlc_
#  vocabulary_placement_v1_0_0.md.
#################################################################

#################################################################
#  v9.76.0 (2026-09-10, brsf-session) -- LINEAGE 9, Objective stage.
#  Consumes Out_Goal_SDLC (629b62f). Status moves to LS_Objectived.
#
#  Five objectives, each measuring one of the three goals with a
#  number taken BEFORE the work (G33: a baseline measured after the
#  work is not a baseline). Every baseline below was counted on the
#  register and the shapes file as they stand at v1.249.0, and the
#  count is stated with the objective so a reader can re-take it.
#
#  The obligations this lineage is building already exist as
#  vocabulary and shapes (TBox v1.90.0, shapes v1.111.0+); what does
#  NOT yet exist is a lineage that owes them -- OS_SDLC_v1 is adopted
#  by no one, because a ruling binds only work that declared it at
#  open (G89, G91). So the measure of this lineage's success is not
#  "the obligations exist" but "a lineage opened under them produces
#  what they demand, and one that does not is refused".
#################################################################



# The baseline readings themselves, as MetricObservations taken today on the register and the shapes
# file at v1.249.0 -- an objective with a target and no reading is a target nobody has taken (L4).



#################################################################
#  v9.77.0 (2026-09-10, brsf-session) -- THE REGISTER ROOT RESTORED,
#  and the archival corrected (G92). backlog_lineage_archive v1.0.0
#  partitioned by reachability with two hand-picked exceptions; the
#  register ROOT belongs to no lineage, so the closure took it, and
#  the live register has had no container since v1.243.0. Measured
