    backlog:hasRationale "Owner's own direct question, 2026-09-15: why are archived lineages subject to current-day shapes? Checked against this tool's own design: backlog_archive_conformance_v1_0_0.py's --seed mode exists exactly for this, grounded in G89/G91 (never apply a ruling retroactively), and had never been run -- every archived lineage, old and new, was being validated as a fresh arrival every gate run, producing 277 false findings, almost entirely artefacts of judging old work under shapes it predates. Seeded once: each of the 14 lineages in the archive (the 13 retired before this session, and L_SDLCObligations, closed this session under the current shapes) is recorded as cleared by the release that closed it, not re-validated against today's rules. Confirmed CONFORMANT after seeding." ;
